{"id": "EUVD-2026-81785", "enisaUuid": "9b28a137-d41b-37d9-b1d7-bcd829c4c1ae", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmailbox: qcom-cpucp: handle NULL data in send_data callback\n\nmailbox_clear_channel() calls mbox_send_message() with NULL data to\nnotify the remote side that the RX channel has been cleared.\nqcom_cpucp_mbox_send_data() blindly dereferenced the data pointer,\ncausing a NULL pointer dereference kernel panic when invoked from\nthis path under PREEMPT_RT.\n\nAdd an explicit NULL check and return early without writing to the\nTX register, which is the correct behaviour for a channel-clear\nnotification.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d11d2a6c9a10de287e0f1b53a5e65d16afe2760", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/413b0b94d6d06b8d49735280e86a01dac90cf177", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3d73e7440e0c40644285be1bda349cdf90122d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc4f2f99530298a1739226947aa76525142d421d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90192", "GHSA-39h4-xrh5-39fg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "349d8978-2062-3e2d-b416-8cf60c4d83d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "38db4799-c4d5-3b1d-8cc6-e25c62ea142a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "4f95054f-9e88-32c8-b1c1-a3f3261feb88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "53babb09-ce99-3986-b5c7-bb8e82613022", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "587d4b7b-7c4d-351a-9a13-102e82474ba5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6354069a-3f83-3a70-8394-43a44fa5498e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Li